  "market_context": "Bitcoin was in a clear downtrend on the 1-hour chart. A consolidation phase formed, which the analyst zoomed into on the 15-minute chart to identify a rising wedge pattern. The break below the wedge confirmed bearish continuation aligned with the higher-time-frame trend.",
  "key_observation": "On the 15-minute BTC/USDT chart, a rising wedge formed during consolidation; its downside breakout—confirmed by a close below the lower trendline and prior market structure—signaled bearish continuation in the context of the dominant downtrend.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified an obvious downtrend on the BTC/USDT 1-hour chart with a consolidation period.",
    "Step 2: Zoomed into the 15-minute timeframe to examine price action details within the consolidation.",
    "Step 3: Recognized a rising wedge pattern on the 15M chart, characterized by higher lows and a descending upper trendline converging toward a breakout point.",
    "Step 4: Noted the breakdown below the rising wedge’s lower trendline, confirming sellers had taken control.",
    "Step 5: Confirmed the break with a close below the previous market structure (swing low), eliminating fake-out risk.",
    "Step 6: Applied Fibonacci retracement to place sell orders at the 0.618 level for precise entry."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "A rising wedge breakdown on a lower timeframe gains high probability when it aligns with the higher-time-frame trend and is confirmed by a close beyond structure—avoid entering before confirmation to filter fakeouts.",
